From 76d510a1d8ac863b05e229a5787552dab7a3c08c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaxdad <atxhxag@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:14:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] feat(egfx): hand copies of presented pixels to the
 presenting decoder

A decoder that presents frames keeps the pixels of the surfaces it was
handed pictures for; the compositor never sees them. A server that decodes
into an offscreen surface and copies it to the one on the output (Remotr's
AVC444 mode copies every frame) therefore got its copies composited from
an empty surface, painting the output black over the video.

The client now tracks which surfaces hold presented pictures, and hands a
SurfaceToSurface from one of them to the decoder (`present_copy`) instead
of the compositor; the destination then holds presented pixels too. The
decoder also hears where each surface is shown (`present_output`, on
MapSurfaceToOutput and the scaled variant, and `None` when a surface is
created or deleted), so it can show only surfaces mapped to the output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
